<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Apum</h1><p class="st-meta">1775 BCE – 1728 BCE (approx.) · capital Shubat-Enlil</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Apum, a north Mesopotamian kingdom ruling from Shamshi-Adad's former capital Shubat-Enlil, until Babylon destroyed it in 1728 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Shubat-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enlil">Enlil</a>, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-leilan">Tell Leilan</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khabur-river">Khabur</a> plains, was the old city of Shehna, renamed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shamshi-adad-i">Shamshi-Adad</a> as the capital of his <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-upper-mesopotamia">Kingdom of Upper Mesopotamia</a>. After his death in the 1770s BCE his realm broke apart, and the city became the seat of the local kingdom of Apum.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its kings, such as Haya-abum and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/till-abnu">Till-Abnu</a>, played the great powers against each other, and their palace archives at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-leilan">Tell Leilan</a> preserve letters and treaties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assur">Assur</a> and other neighbours. The kingdom depended on rain-fed barley farming and the trade routes across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khabur-river">Khabur</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/babylonian-empire">Babylonian Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samsu-iluna">Samsu-iluna</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi's</a> son, sacked Shubat-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enlil">Enlil</a> in 1728 BCE and ended the kingdom. The city was abandoned, and excavations by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yale-university">Yale University</a> from 1979 recovered its archives.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1775 BCE – 1728 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:24.38%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1775 BCE – 1728 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century-bce">18th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Shubat-Enlil</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Haya-abum, Till-Abnu, Yakun-ashar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Mesopotamian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Amorite, Akkadian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Apum, Shubat-Enlil, Shehna</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1752&amp;focus=apum" aria-label="Apum on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5650 911 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Apum lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6092 1134h0M6143 1252h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5970 1167h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5970 1167h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Syria. <a href="/atlas?year=-1752&amp;focus=apum">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
